WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.440
Many organizations generate SBOMs during software builds, release processes,

00:00:04.440 --> 00:00:06.000
and deployment activities.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:10.420
Integrating SBOM generation into development workflows can improve consistency and reduce

00:00:10.420 --> 00:00:11.000
manual effort.

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:15.560
The software development lifecycle is a natural place to create SBOMs because build

00:00:15.560 --> 00:00:17.000
systems often know which packages,

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:20.000
libraries, containers, and artifacts were included in a release.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:21.920
Automation helps keep SBOMs current.

00:00:21.920 --> 00:00:25.000
If an SBOM is generated every time software is built or released,

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:27.961
the inventory is more likely to reflect what was actually delivered.

00:00:27.961 --> 00:00:31.000
SBOMs can also be stored with release artifacts.

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:34.130
This makes it easier to connect a product version to the components that were present at

00:00:34.130 --> 00:00:35.250
the time of release.

00:00:35.250 --> 00:00:38.000
Development teams can use SBOMs to review dependency changes.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:39.905
A new package, major version change,

00:00:39.905 --> 00:00:44.225
or unexpected transitive dependency may deserve additional review before release.

00:00:44.225 --> 00:00:48.382
Security teams can use SBOM outputs to enrich vulnerability management and software risk

00:00:48.382 --> 00:00:49.346
workflows.

00:00:49.346 --> 00:00:53.250
Compliance teams may use the same data to support evidence requests or customer assurance

00:00:53.250 --> 00:00:54.000
processes.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:57.240
The practical lesson is to make SBOM generation part of how software is built and

00:00:57.240 --> 00:00:58.000
maintained.

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:00.035
When SBOMs are embedded in the lifecycle,

00:01:00.035 --> 00:01:04.000
they become living operational artifacts rather than occasional documents.

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:07.000
Teams should also decide how SBOMs are versioned and retained.

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:11.000
Being able to connect a released product version to the SBOM generated for that release

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:14.000
can be critical during vulnerability response or customer assurance work.

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:15.920
Lifecycle integration also makes ownership clearer.

00:01:15.920 --> 00:01:24.000
If each product team knows where its SBOMs are created, stored, and reviewed,

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:24.770
software transparency becomes a repeatable engineering practice rather than an occasional

00:01:24.770 --> 00:01:25.286
special request.
